FINDING 1 — dismiss, then a mutation that clears the warning, then the SAME
warning set reappears: live region re-announces but the banner never comes back.
Sequence: (1) load with warning W1/key K1 -> banner visible, region says
"Pattern overlap warning: ...". (2) user dismisses -> sessionStorage[dismissed]=K1,
banner removed, region says "Account overlap warning dismissed.",
lastWarningsText is NOT updated (stays W1's text, by design per the code comment).
(3) an intervening mutation clears the overlap (Warnings=[], key="") -> region
text differs from lastWarningsText, so region.textContent is overwritten to ""
and lastWarningsText is reset to "". (4) the identical warning set W1/K1
reappears (e.g. user edits a FilePatterns field back to what it was) -> server
re-renders the banner (Warnings non-empty) AND the region text; syncWarnings()
sees text ("Pattern overlap warning: ...") != lastWarningsText ("") so it WRITES
the warning text into the live region (a fresh aria-live announcement to screen
readers) -- but then, in the same call, sees sessionStorage[dismissed] === K1
and immediately banner.remove()s the just-rendered banner.
Observed (harness output):
  Step 4: region.textContent = "Pattern overlap warning: acct-1 and acct-2 both
  match statement-2026.csv"; banner present after sync? false
Required (per the worker's own design comment on WarningsKey: "a changed warning
set is never mistaken for one already dismissed" -- implying an UNCHANGED set
must stay uniformly dismissed): a screen-reader user gets an aria-live
announcement asserting an active pattern-overlap warning exists, with no banner,
no dismiss button, and nothing in the DOM to act on -- while a sighted user sees
nothing at all. This is exactly the "announcement asserting a state that is not
current" failure mode the task brief asked me to look for, and it is
reachable by an ordinary user workflow (revert a pattern edit).

FINDING 2 — full page reload after a dismissal, warnings unchanged: the live
region permanently asserts a warning that the banner never shows.
Sequence: (1) dismiss W1/K1 in a session (sessionStorage[dismissed]=K1).
(2) reload the page (F5, or open a new tab that inherits sessionStorage) while
the SAME overlap (W1/K1) is still present. On a full page GET, both the
#accounts-warnings-region block and the #accounts-list partial (with the
banner) are server-rendered directly from the unchanged .Warnings/.WarningsKey
-- this is not conditioned on the dismissal at all, since the dismissal state
lives only in the browser's sessionStorage, not in any request the server
sees. So the region's template server-renders "Pattern overlap warning: ..."
inline into the sr-only node, and the banner also server-renders. The <script>
then seeds `lastWarningsText` from the region's own already-rendered text
(line ~132: `var lastWarningsText = region ? region.textContent : ''`), so on
the first syncWarnings() call text === lastWarningsText and the same-text
guard is FALSE -- the region is left untouched, i.e. left containing
"Pattern overlap warning: ..." -- while the banner is immediately removed
because sessionStorage still matches K1.
Observed (harness output, Scenario 2):
  region.textContent on load = "Pattern overlap warning: acct-1 and acct-2 both
  match statement-2026.csv"; banner present = false
This is not a rare interleaving -- it is triggered by the single most common
action on any web page (reload), immediately after the one interaction the
banner itself offers (dismiss). It persists indefinitely: nothing will touch
the region again until the warning content actually changes. Any assistive
technology that reads page content directly (not only live-region-triggered
announcements -- e.g. browsing/scanning modes, or simply navigating to the
region's landmark) will find "Pattern overlap warning: ..." text sitting in
the accessibility tree with no corresponding visible or interactive element
anywhere on the page. ACCESSIBILITY.md point 14 requires banners to be
"re-announced only on state change, not every page load within a session" --
the implicit companion requirement, that the announced state matches what is
actually presented, is violated: state has NOT changed (same key, still
dismissed) yet the on-load DOM permanently disagrees with the banner about
whether a warning is showing.

Both findings trace to the same root cause the task brief predicted: the
dismiss handler updates sessionStorage (content-keyed) but deliberately does
NOT update lastWarningsText (raw-text-keyed), and the two independently
gate two different things (live-region write vs. banner visibility) that the
template's own comments assume move together ("does not re-announce or
re-show on every load while unchanged, but does reappear the moment the set
of warnings changes" -- reappear and re-announce are supposed to be the same
event; they are not).

Other angles attacked and NOT found broken:
- warningsKey collisions: FNV-64a over sorted warnings joined with a NUL
  separator between each element (internal/handlers/accounts/handlers.go,
  warningsKey()) rules out the classic concatenation-ambiguity collision
  (e.g. ["ab","c"] vs ["a","bc"]) since "ab\0c" != "a\0bc\0"... actually the
  code appends a trailing 0 byte after every element including the last, so
  the hash input is unambiguous per-element; did not find a practical
  collision path via ordinary warning text (warning strings are built from
  account IDs/basenames, which cannot contain NUL on any real filesystem).
- Scope creep: none -- diff confined to the three manifest files.
- Debug instrumentation: none found.
- TestHandlePage_RendererMode_NoOverlapRendersNoWarningBlock: not vacuous --
  legitimately asserts no "Pattern overlap warning" substring anywhere when
  Warnings is empty, which is true for the region/data-node text too since
  they're gated by the same {{if .Warnings}}.
- Focus target #accounts-new-heading: exists on both full-page and every
  accounts-list-partial swap (it is rendered unconditionally in the same
  partial as the banner), so the dismiss handler's focus() call has a real
  target in every response shape reachable through this code path.

